## HOW TO CALCULATE EACH SECTION

### 1. DDI Agency Rate (What Client Pays DDI)

**Source:** `DEE_DAVIS_INC_COMPLETE_SERVICE_CATALOG.md`

If the RFP specifies quantities and DDI has published agency rates → use those rates.

If the RFP is "best value" or allows DDI to set pricing → use catalog rates as the baseline, adjust for competition level and contract size.

If the RFP is "lowest price" (LPTA) → estimate competitive market rates, back into DDI's margin.

### 2. Fulfillment Cost (What DDI Pays Subs)

**Source:** `DDI_BUSINESS_MODEL.md` margin targets + known partner pricing

| Service Type | Target Margin | Fulfillment Cost Estimate |
|---|---|---|
| Drug Testing | 25-40% | Agency rate × 0.60-0.75 |
| Fingerprinting | 40-60% | Agency rate × 0.40-0.60 |
| DNA Testing | 40-60% | Agency rate × 0.40-0.60 |
| NEMT | 20-35% | Agency rate × 0.65-0.80 |
| Janitorial | 20-30% | Agency rate × 0.70-0.80 |
| Landscaping | 20-30% | Agency rate × 0.70-0.80 |
| Staffing | 25-40% | Agency rate × 0.60-0.75 |
| Freight/Logistics | 25-40% | Agency rate × 0.60-0.75 |
| Delivery/Courier | 25-40% | Agency rate × 0.60-0.75 |
| Construction | 15-25% | Agency rate × 0.75-0.85 |
| IT Services | 25-35% | Agency rate × 0.65-0.75 |
| Consulting/PE | 60-80% | Agency rate × 0.20-0.40 |

If actual sub quotes are in hand → use actual numbers, not estimates.

### 3. Win Probability

| Factor | High (70-90%) | Medium (40-60%) | Low (10-30%) |
|---|---|---|---|
| Set-Aside | EDWOSB sole source or set-aside | WOSB or SB set-aside | Full & open |
| Competition | <5 likely bidders | 5-15 bidders | 15+ bidders |
| Experience | 3+ similar contracts won | 1-2 similar | First time in this lane |
| Relationship | Know the CO, prior work | Submitted questions/email | Cold |
| Geography | Local/regional presence | Can establish presence | Far from service area |
| Sub Ready | Sub confirmed with pricing | Sub identified, no pricing | No sub yet |

**Estimated Win % = Average of all factor scores**

### 4. Bid Prep Effort

| Bid Complexity | Estimated Hours | Estimated Cost (@$125/hr) |
|---|---|---|
| Micro-purchase / simple quote | 2-5 hrs | $250-$625 |
| Standard RFQ / cap statement | 5-10 hrs | $625-$1,250 |
| Full RFP with forms | 15-30 hrs | $1,875-$3,750 |
| Complex proposal (technical + price) | 30-60 hrs | $3,750-$7,500 |
| Major IDIQ / multi-volume | 60-120 hrs | $7,500-$15,000 |

### 5. Revenue Tier Definitions

| Tier | Annual Revenue to DDI | Typical Contract Types |
|---|---|---|
| **Micro-Purchase** | Under $10K/yr | One-time supply orders, small quotes |
| **Small** | $10K-$50K/yr | Local service contracts, small recurring orders |
| **Medium** | $50K-$250K/yr | County/state RFPs, multi-location drug testing, grounds maintenance |
| **Large** | $250K-$1M/yr | Federal IDIQs, state-wide service contracts, NEMT programs |
| **Major** | $1M+/yr | Multi-year federal contracts, large NEMT brokerage, staffing programs |

### 6. Verdict Logic

| Verdict | Criteria |
|---|---|
| **STRONG BID** | Margin ≥ target + win probability ≥ 50% + sub ready + ROI > 10x |
| **WORTH PURSUING** | Margin ≥ target + win probability ≥ 30% + ROI > 5x |
| **MARGINAL** | Margin below target OR win probability < 30% OR ROI < 5x |
| **PASS** | Margin < 15% OR no sub available OR ROI < 2x OR can't meet requirements |

